Use this page to publish notable registry updates, new items, breaking changes, and migration notes.

---

## Current catalog

**Components:** `accordion`, `badge`, `button`, `card`, `tabs`
**Blocks:** `announcement-bar`, `hero`
**Utilities:** `cn`, `styles`

Each is published as installable JSON under `/r/<name>.json`, with a live preview on its docs page and a matching Storybook story. See [Registry](/docs/registry) for how items are authored.

### Component install path

- UI components now install into `components/<name>/` at the consumer project root (`~/components/button`, `~/components/badge`, …) instead of `src/lib/components/ui/<name>`.

### CLI install commands

- Install commands now use the item JSON URL. shadcn-svelte does not support namespaced aliases like `@design-system-ui/styles`.
- Bun install examples use `bun x shadcn-svelte@latest add …`.

### Styles install path

- The `styles` item now installs into `styles/` at the consumer project root (`~/styles/*.css`) instead of next to the project's Tailwind CSS file.

### Styles authoring

- The `styles` item now keeps `_registry.svx`, `_preview.svelte`, and the published CSS together in `registry/items/files/styles`. It still shows under [Utilities](/utilities/styles).

### Styles docs

- The [Styles](/docs/styles) page now matches the published `styles` item: four files in `styles/` at the project root, and the secondary/tertiary `data-theme` presets.

### Styles

- The `styles` utility now publishes the CSS in `registry/items/files/styles` (`globals.css` plus the default, secondary, and tertiary theme presets). Install it before components so semantic tokens resolve.

### Docs shell

- Sidebar navigation rebuilt to match the shadcn-svelte `sidebar-07` pattern: one flat, collapsible menu per top-level section (Docs, Components, Blocks, Utilities), closing fully flush rather than leaving an icon rail.
- "Copy Page" and previous/next navigation moved into the page header as compact icon controls.
- Section breadcrumbs link to the section's first page instead of a non-navigable overview route.
